# Line endings — one policy for everyone, regardless of OS or local git config.
#
# Why this file exists: vercel.json and server.mjs pin a SHA-256 hash of the
# inline theme-init script in index.html for the Content-Security-Policy. A
# hash is over raw BYTES, so an LF (\n) file and a CRLF (\r\n) file with
# identical text produce different hashes. If index.html is ever committed
# with CRLF, the browser refuses to run the theme script and dark mode
# silently stops restoring on reload. Pinning eol=lf makes that impossible.
#
# eol=lf checks files out as LF on every platform, so a Windows clone gets
# the same bytes as macOS, Linux and the Vercel build. It overrides each
# developer's core.autocrlf setting — nobody has to configure anything.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, because these carry the CSP hash and the sync'd copy of it.
index.html text eol=lf
vercel.json text eol=lf
server.mjs  text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch the bytes, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff2 binary
